+{"body":"We need a way to convert markdown in a draft of habr article using browser automation so it will allow us to safe time, and make upload precise.\n\nFor example the page of latest version of our article is:\nhttps://habr.com/ru/article/edit/1018142\n\nAnd here the html markup of it: https://gist.githubusercontent.com/konard/23f6cb2453bf2756679dbb5298e908cb/raw/dbcd5de8956b9eb021113de1f3a68e772245dac7/habr-article-editor-page.html\n\nSee https://github.com/link-foundation/browser-commander\n\nMake sure we have nice docs on how to use the tool.\n\nWe need to have ability to download article state from read only state, download it from edit form, double check everything matches exactly, and apply the changes from source markdown document, so we can simplify editing of our article at habr.\n\nWe need to collect data related about the issue to this repository, make sure we compile that data to `./docs/case-studies/issue-{id}` folder, and use it to do deep case study analysis (also make sure to search online for additional facts and data), list of each and all requirements from the issue, and propose possible solutions and solution plans for each requirement (we should also check known existing components/libraries, that solve similar problem or can help in solutions).\n\nPlease plan and execute everything in this single pull request, you have unlimited time and context, as context auto-compacts and you can continue indefinitely, until it is each and every requirement fully addressed, and everything is totally done.","comments":[],"title":"Article uploader using browser-commander","updatedAt":"2026-06-05T20:11:09Z"}
